  "prompt": "Is filing the individual annual income tax return on May 15 already late?",
  "attempt": 1,
  "runtimeCommit": "22b845afe1fe16bfa4821804d528f469366e4f8c",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, filing the individual annual income tax return on May 15 is considered late. The deadline for filing the return is April 15 of each year.\n\n### Interpretation\nThe NIRC specifies that taxpayers must file their income tax returns on or before April 15. Filing after this date, such as on May 15, constitutes a late filing, which may subject the taxpayer to penalties and interest on any taxes due.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nTaxpayers who file their individual annual income tax returns after April 15 should be aware of the potential for incurring penalties and interest charges. It is advisable to file on time to avoid these additional costs.",
